PHASE I: UEFI-ROOT AND RING -1 SUBSTRATE (A-HVS)\uc0\u8232 To eliminate the "fat and noisy" interference of standard kernels, Axion initializes as a UEFI DXE (Driver Execution Environment) driver.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Pre-Kernel Virtualization (VMX-Root)\
Axion takes control of the Global Descriptor Table (GDT) and Interrupt Descriptor Table (IDT) before the OS bootloader. It activates VMX-Root mode, creating a persistent Hyper-Isolator.\
Logic: The host OS is "trapped" in a non-root partition. Every hardware request from the OS (I/O, IRQ, MSR) is intercepted via VM-Exits and queued or delayed based on the Axion compute heartbeat.\
B. SMM-Jailing and SMI-Trap\
System Management Interrupts (SMIs) are usually invisible to the OS. At the UEFI level, Axion locks the SMI-configuration to ensure all hardware-level interrupts are routed through the SMI-Trap.\
Equation 7: Jitter-Free Window (W_jf)\
W_jf = T_cycle - (T_SMM_delay + T_VM-Exit_overhead)\
This allows Axion to defer "noisy" motherboard telemetry (fan control, battery checks) until the 165 GFLOPS compute pulse has completed its cycle.\
